WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:08.441
Start the day knowing how yesterday went. The daily brief puts every location on one screen, with the few things worth acting on first.

2
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:20.797
Open Operations, and choose Daily brief. At the top are yesterday’s totals: sales against the same day last week, labour hours and sales per hour, and food safety checks done.

3
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:29.724
What needs you lists up to six things, most urgent first, like a food safety problem, stock to order now, missed checks, or a big drop in sales.

4
00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:37.484
Below, each location gets its own card, with its sales, labour, food safety, stock, tickets, and who’s on today.

5
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:45.400
To get it every morning, turn on Every morning, pick the time, and choose email, your phone, or both. It’s in your own time zone.

6
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:52.992
Send me one now shows you what it looks like. Each person sets their own, and the brief only shows what they’re allowed to see.

7
00:00:54.067 --> 00:01:03.069
Every headline links to the screen that fixes it. This one opens the inventory suggestions for Downtown, to sort out the avocados and oat milk.

8
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:12.120
That’s the daily brief. Next in the Features series: shifts. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

